GraphTask
=========

GraphTask runs BBC BASIC programs in windows on the desktop, instead of
taking over the whole screen. Each program gets a "graphics task
window" of its own, with its own screen mode and colours, and carries
on while you use other programs. It is after David Ruck's !GraphTask
(1990-2021).

Double-click !GraphTask to put its icon on the right of the icon bar.

  SELECT on the icon    a window at BASIC's > prompt (type RUN,
                        CHAIN "name", MODE 7, *Cat...)
  Drag a BASIC file     to the icon: it runs in a window of its own
  MENU on the icon      Info, New task, Choices..., Quit

Click in a window to give it the keyboard: keys (and INKEY) only reach
the program whose window has the input focus. Escape stops it; the
window keeps its last picture. Close a window whose program is still
running and GraphTask asks before killing it.

MENU over a window gives its menu:

  Menu button     MENU clicks go to the program (MOUSE sees 2);
                  Shift-MENU still opens this menu
  Suspend/Resume  pause the program and carry on
  Kill            stop it (the picture stays)
  Restart         run it again from the start
  Speed           ARM2, ARM3, ARM610, StrongARM (the default) or
                  Unlimited
  Scale           1:1, x2 or Fit window
  Full screen     the whole screen (Alt-Return); Alt-Return again
                  goes back to the window
  Save screen     the picture as a Sprite file

You can also Shift-drag the picture (with SELECT) to a directory
display to save it as a sprite.

Choices... sets the speed and scale new windows start with, the mode a
> prompt window starts in, and "Double-click runs BASIC in a window":
when that is on, double-clicking a BASIC file runs it in a window while
GraphTask is loaded (normally it runs full screen, as in RISC OS 3.71).

Commands, for Obey files and applications' !Run files too:

  *GraphTask <file> [<arguments>]   run a program in a window
  *GraphTask                        a window at the > prompt
  *BASIC -window <file>             the same
  Run <GraphTask$Dir> <files>       each file in a window of its own

!JsEdit's Run runs a BASIC listing in a graphics task window, and the
Task Manager's menu has "Graphics task window".

Programs that call Wimp_Initialise become ordinary desktop tasks and
leave their window.
